xnu 0194: the keepalive at cp_start must use the local gmu handle

0190 added the keepalive raise next to the "cp started" log, testing
mondrian_uc_gmu -- which is only assigned ~200 lines later. The block therefore
never ran: the ring from that boot has no "cp keepalive held up" line, and the
parked-GPU hypothesis (a GPU idle for minutes before CoreAnimation's first
frame) is still untested. Use the local handle the function already has.

--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
@@ -2436,8 +2436,8 @@
 	 * GPU and the CP never fetches it (CP_RB_RPTR stays at CP_RB_WPTR).
 	 * gpukeep=1 keeps it up from here on.
 	 */
-	if (mondrian_uc_gmu != 0 && mondrian_uc_keep == 1) {
-		mondrian_gpu_write(mondrian_uc_gmu, GMU_OFF(0x1f8c3u), 1);
+	if (gmu != 0 && mondrian_uc_keep == 1) {
+		mondrian_gpu_write(gmu, GMU_OFF(0x1f8c3u), 1);
 		printf("MONDRIAN GPU: cp keepalive held up\n");
 		mondrian_log_flush_now();
 	}
